{
  "summary": "Adds a `ReconstructMultipath` method to the `Descriptor` class, allowing an ordered set of single-path expanded descriptors to be recombined into their original unified multipath `Descriptor` object. Refactors BIP32 keypath handling to represent derivation steps as `KeyPathElement` and `KeyPath` objects that store hardening and multipath information, and updates `Parse` to return a single multipath `Descriptor`.",
  "problem": "Multipath descriptors expand into distinct single-path descriptors, but there is no programmatic way to reverse this expansion and recover the combined multipath descriptor object from the expanded siblings.",
  "evidence": [
   "PR description: 'This expansion is reversible - given the expansion in the order of the multipath elements, it is possible to determine what the original multipath descriptor was. This PR adds ReconstructMultipath to produce a new Descriptor representing the multipath descriptor that produced the expansion.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [
      "#36442"
    ],
    "enables": [
      "#36444"
    ]
  },
  "scope_notes": "Includes commits from base PR #36442 refactoring Parse() and keypath representation in util/bip32. Large diff touching descriptor internals, wallet parsing, and RPC callers.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Now includes base commits from #36442 refactoring `ParseHDKeypath`, `KeyPathElement`, and changing `Parse` to return a single descriptor instead of a vector.",
  "card": "Adds ReconstructMultipath to rebuild a unified multipath Descriptor object from an ordered set of expanded single-path descriptors. It also refactors BIP32 keypath parsing into dedicated KeyPathElement and KeyPath classes capable of handling multipath derivation steps. The feature is verified via unit tests and fuzzing round-trips. Depends on #36442 and is required by #36444.",
